@forfrossen, answers to your two scope questions on #5079:

1. **Direction 2 (W030 `/gsd-health` budget).** Approved: split it out. Open a separate enhancement issue for the budget warning, gated on #5121 bounding the `SKILL.md` read, and #5079 may close this issue without it.
2. **Spawn-prompt lines.** Not approved within this issue. The removals in `execute-phase.md`, `execute-phase/steps/executor-isolation-dispatch.md`, `plan-phase.md`, `quick.md` and the `plan-pre` fragment (with the regenerated `capability-registry.cjs`) go into their own PR and issue; keep #5079 to the agent-side change approved on 2026-09-26.

@forfrossen #5079 was closed as stale on 2026-10-21, after trek-e's 2026-10-14 rulings on it: dropping step 3 (the `agent_skills` dedup) is approved, and Major 5 and Minor 5 of review 5477758996 are closed by maintainer decision. Findings that exist only because of step 3 fall away with it; the rest of that review still applies. trek-e's closing note invites a reopen or a new PR.

Do you plan to pick it back up? If you'd rather hand it off, say so here and I'll ask for it to be reassigned. Either way, the split-out work stays separate: #5248 (the spawn-prompt lines) and #5249 (the `/gsd-health` warning). #5249 is gated on #5121, which closed on 2026-10-17, and also depends on the scoped read this issue adds.

